Roots of |phi(B)|=0 and |theta(B)|=0 (moduli; > 1 is stationary/invertible):

  AR (Phi)          inf    1.79940    1.79940    1.10196 
  MA (Theta)    2.57261    0.99996*

  * A root sits on the unit circle -- an MA root (modulus 0.99996).  The
    likelihood rose towards a non-invertible MA and the optimiser stopped
    at the engine's invertibility gate: this is a CONSTRAINED point, not an
    interior maximum.  The standard errors of the MA are not defined along
    that direction, and no LR that uses this fit has its usual
    distribution (BUG-49).
    The combination the model differences once too often -- the left
    null vector u of Theta*(1), smallest singular value 4.55e-06 -- has
    weights (|u|, on Ybar = [nabla Y2 ; W]):
      nabla muskrat        0.8982
      W1                   0.4395
    It lies in the nabla Y2 block (share 0.81): that combination of the
    common-trend series looks OVER-DIFFERENCED -- stationary in levels.
    Read it as evidence that the rank is higher than 1, or that the
    series in that block are not I(1).


